RISC3D test kit 25 (prototype, 14 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 24's results: leaving out TORCS's glHint changed nothing (the
picture was identical). Leaving out mipmaps made the scenery sharper,
but the car stayed plain yellow and the trees stayed striped. So
mipmaps are not the main fault.

The fault looks like texture coordinates going wrong on the GPU: the
car drawn with one colour from its texture, the trees and grass
stretched in one direction. TORCS gives its coordinates from its own
memory, and since 0.9 rol-3d gives them to Mesa as memory too, where
the Pi's GPU driver copies them itself (software Mesa doesn't need to).
This kit redraws the recording on the GPU with rol-3d putting them into
buffers itself instead, as 0.8 did.

Nothing to install: the package stays riscos-risc3d 0.13-1 (from kit
24). Only the replay script is new.

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 24.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell:
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/replay /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d 240
    It writes ReplayGPU-240, ReplayBuffers-240, ReplayBufNoMip-240 and
    ReplaySoft-240 (PPM pictures) into RISC3DTest. It sets
    /riscos/3d/uploads for the two buffer runs and puts it back after.

